.el .ds Aq '
.TH tfa 1  "tfa v0.1.1" 
.SH NAME
tfa \- CLI Two\-Factor Authentication (2FA) tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtfa\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-storage\fR] [\fB\-\-clipboard\fR] [\fB\-\-clip\-command\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-namespace\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CLI Two\-Factor Authentication (2FA) tool
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to configuration file (TOML, YAML, or JSON)
.TP
\fB\-\-storage\fR \fI<STORAGE>\fR
Credential storage backend
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Attempt OS keyring first; fallback to local file store if unavailable
.IP \(bu 2
keyring: Strictly use system keyring (Secret Service, Keychain, Credential Manager)
.IP \(bu 2
file: Use local file storage (~/.local/share/tfa/credentials.json)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-clipboard\fR \fI<CLIPBOARD>\fR
Clipboard copy provider (system or osc52)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
system: Native system clipboard (arboard with Wayland/X11/macOS/Windows)
.IP \(bu 2
osc52: Terminal ANSI escape sequence OSC 52 (works over remote SSH, tmux, screen)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-clip\-command\fR \fI<CLIP_COMMAND>\fR
Custom clipboard command to receive token via standard input (e.g. wl\-copy, pbcopy, xclip)
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-namespace\fR \fI<NAMESPACE>\fR
Target namespace for account scoping (e.g. personal, work, home)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tfa\-generate(1)
Generate a 2FA token (TOTP, Steam, or HOTP) for an account
.TP
tfa\-instant(1)
Generate a 2FA token instantly from raw secret, URI, or stdin without storage
.TP
tfa\-watch(1)
Live watch mode displaying continuous TOTP countdown with progress bar
.TP
tfa\-add(1)
Add a new account secret or OTPAuth URL
.TP
tfa\-qr(1)
Render account as a terminal QR code for mobile authenticator scanning
.TP
tfa\-list(1)
List all stored accounts or live token status
.TP
tfa\-status(1)
Live overview status dashboard of all accounts and tokens (alias for list \-\-codes)
.TP
tfa\-delete(1)
Delete an account secret
.TP
tfa\-rename(1)
Rename an account within the active namespace
.TP
tfa\-move(1)
Move an account to a different namespace
.TP
tfa\-show(1)
Show account details and stored secret
.TP
tfa\-export(1)
Export accounts to an encrypted backup file or stdout
.TP
tfa\-import(1)
Import accounts from a backup file, migration URI, or JSON payload
.TP
tfa\-completions(1)
Generate shell autocompletions script
.TP
tfa\-man(1)
Generate UNIX roff man page
.TP
tfa\-namespace(1)
Manage and isolate accounts across multi\-tenant namespaces
.TP
tfa\-password(1)
Manage master password protection and unlock sessions
.TP
tfa\-audit(1)
Scan stored accounts and credentials file for security vulnerabilities
.TP
tfa\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
vv0.1.1
